20,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our lab is severely understaffed, and our volunteers are mostly from the history circle. We must be careful with the workload.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Shion,,"We've had several openings slip due to paperwork delays, and powered displays are prone to breaking down during gallery hours.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,May,,People love it when there's a human presence or a mechanism moving. Static cases just don't bring them back for a second visit.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and our evening hires mean we can't have fragile, open arrangements that can't be moved.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Transport costs are huge—nearly a third of installation! Also, bespoke mounts are getting very expensive. We need things that come with their own supports.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, that is a worrying cost. Perhaps we should look for something that doesn't require so many expensive loans.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@May, if mechanisms attract crowds but break often, we are trading popularity for a lot of stress and roped-off areas.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, but the data shows that's what the visitors want. We just need a reliable way to do it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, if the lab is backed up, we certainly cannot afford an exhibition that requires heavy conservation work on-site.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, does that mean we should avoid heavy things? I don't want the floor to break!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. We need a project that utilizes our history-loving volunteers without overloading the lone conservation officer.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Shion,,We should avoid complex overseas loans with tight cut-offs and high-maintenance electronics if we want a smooth season.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,May,,"I still think a ""living"" exhibition is the way to go. Something with people working or talking in the room.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Misaki,,Exactly. And it must be light enough for the bay and flexible enough for the evening caterers to pass through.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"So, no heavy stones and no fancy expensive mounts! Let's find something simple but fun.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
